+---
+id: task-003-fix-applypatch-conformance-to-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "Fix applyPatch conformance to RFC 6902"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## What was done
+
+Reviewed how `applyPatch` validates and applies patches against RFC 6902 and fixed two deviations in
+`src/index.ts`, tests first in `src/index.test.ts`:
+
+- A patch array with holes (`new Array(2)`, `[op, , op]`) was accepted and the holes silently skipped.
+  Holes are now read as `undefined` and rejected with `TypeError`, like any non-object operation.
+- `replace` was a removal plus an addition, which moved an object member to the end. It now overwrites
+  the value in place: key order is kept, arrays keep their length.
+
+Everything else checked (move into own child, move onto itself, `-` handling, array index grammar,
+`test` equality, atomicity, non-mutation) already conformed. See dl-003.
